  message: "Done in PR #3487. 17 production emit sites across 12 linkers/analyzers folded per ADR-0025's rename table (routes_to/delegates_to/annotated_dispatches/uses_dispatch_table/di_registers/di_resolves/registers_routes/message_dispatch/crdt_publishes/annotated_publishes/emits/enqueues). The event_subscribes producer in event_sourcing.py is dropped entirely per the DEPRECATE-NO-FOLD verdict (subscriber-is-enclosed-by-method information is recoverable from Symbol.span; same verdict pattern as message_receive in ADR-0026). Consumer-side updates: compact.CROSS_CUTTING_EDGE_TYPES adds 'calls' + 'event_publishes'; bakeoff-deep _CALL_FLOW_EDGE_TYPES + routes_to filter rewritten to canonical+meta query; bakeoff-broad route-edge detection rewritten; hypergumbo_diag.py routes_to filter rewritten. 12 linker test files updated via replace_all; TestEventSubscriberToMethodEdges class rewritten to assert the producer-drop sticks. 3512 tests passing, 100% coverage on all 13 changed source files. Tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: dispatch-heavy / route-heavy / pub-sub-heavy repos (Spring, Express, Rails ActiveJob, NestJS, Yjs, gRPC, Solidity) should see the canonical-fold's centrality/slice/sketch implications confirmed by a DEEP cycle."  # 5c8a
